A||||13||JayUSA77||need help with lock cylinder||||4||
Z||000000||JayUSA77||07-22-2001||03:06 PM||||Hey guys,<BR>my locks in my car are close to gone and i dont want them to go before i change them. But there is one problem i cant figure out how.  I looked through the book and it didnt say.  I was thinking about taking the outer body panel off but that seems like too much.  I took off all my interior panels and can see the lock cylinder but i can figure out how it comes off.  All i need to do it pull the old one off and get the new one on. ANY help would be greatly appreciated because this is a major pain in my A$$. Thanks guys<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||4
Z||000001||fiero56||07-22-2001||03:58 PM||||take off inner door panel, remove "c" clip holding the cylinder in place, and pull it out. You might have to remove outer door panel rub strip, I can't remember. Its a simple job.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JayUSA77||07-22-2001||05:09 PM||||does this C clip come right out or do i need some kind of special tool.<BR>and oh ya thanks.<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||07-22-2001||05:22 PM||||There's a 90' tab, use needle nose pliers or a screwdriver.  Make sure you don't drop the clip down in the door.  I used a piece of tape to hold mine while the lock cylinder was out.<P>Getting the clip back on is the hardest part.  May take a few tries.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||07-22-2001||05:42 PM||||Gettign the clip in is the hardest part. It typically takes a few minutes the first time you do it, then the second door takes just a minute. And keep a rag handy for the in-evitable cut(s) from the door. I have yet to work inside those doors and not leave the project with permanent battle scars. My record so far is a scar(still there) 1.5" long from installing power windows, I bled everywhere for hours after that.||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||07-22-2001||06:31 PM||||You will need to remove the rear part of the body molding to get to the black plastic standoff. It is way easier if you pull it out.<BR>Dont worry about droping the clip. Just reach in and get it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||JayUSA77||07-22-2001||06:46 PM||||alright guys check this, i just pulled out the damn lock right, but the outer part stayed in.  Which way does this thing come out, do i push it in towards the car or do i pull it out away from the car.  I tried a screwdriver and hammer without luck.  I have everything out except the base of the lock. Damnit this sucks, any extra info would be appreciated.<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||JayUSA77||07-22-2001||06:59 PM||||and oh ya i forgot to mention, Is there a lock that holds this think in place because i havent loosened anything i know of.<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||07-22-2001||07:05 PM||||If the base of the cylinder will not move...you did remove the "c" clip, right?||||reg||1
Z||000009||JayUSA77||07-22-2001||07:07 PM||||Is the "C" clip the metal thing surrounding the entire lock.  That metal piece seems to connect to a couple things how do i remove it.?????Thanks<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||07-22-2001||07:24 PM||||what there call a 'C' clip is a piece of flat metal a couple of inches square that has a small right angle bend in it. The opposite side has a 'C' shaped cut out. grab the bent up edge with pliers or pry with a screwdriver towards the back edge of door till it is past the little tabs on the lock cylinder. then just push the whole cylinder out from the inside toward the outside. when its far enough out disconnect the metal rod linkage (its got a little plastic clip) turn the clip a 1/4 turn to pop it off the rod and the rod will come out. Install is the opposite. If you cant figure it out i can post you a pic of the parts.||||reg||1
Z||000011||JayUSA77||07-22-2001||08:50 PM||||Thanks guys, i now have a new driver side lock installed plus the battle scars to prove it.  now i got another problem my window is messed up. Well im about to start another chat, thanks again, my problems have been solved, or at least one of them <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000012||cadaver||07-23-2001||12:34 AM||||your window is messed up? what did you do?||||reg||1
Z||000013||JayUSA77||07-23-2001||01:22 AM||||i dont know but now it is leaning towards the car alot more than it was, i figured out how to fix it though, i have to adjust some bolts located at the top of the door..Thanks cadaver<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
